# Draft knowledge entry: libb64 2.0.0 upstream examples make test missing library target (OHOS test workflow)
id: DRAFT-libb64-2.0.0-upstream-make-test-missing-library-target
trigger_tool: make|clang|test-package
phase: testing|validation|portability
error_signature: "No rule to make target 'libb64.a', needed by 'c-example1'|make test.*Stop|missing library target in examples Makefile"

severity: 2
category: testing|ohos|makefile|portability
match_keywords: libb64, base64, examples Makefile, make test, libb64.a, missing target, upstream test entry, OHOS, clang, test ledger

title: libb64 2.0.0 upstream examples `make test` assumes prebuilt libb64.a; preserve the failed entry and replace it with an equivalent API-calling clang test plus ledger on OHOS
root_cause: >
  upstream examples/Makefile declares `test: test-c-example1 test-c-example2` and
  `c-example1 c-example2: libb64.a`, but the build graph provides no rule that
  produces libb64.a within that target invocation (the archive is built by
  src/Makefile, not by examples/Makefile). In a clean source tree on OHOS,
  `make test` therefore exits 2 with "No rule to make target 'libb64.a'".
affected_scope: >
  Any upstream Makefile whose test target assumes a prebuilt library archive
  that the same target invocation does not build, especially under a clean
  OHOS/OpenHarmony source tree (libb64 2.0.0 demonstrated case).
verification_cmd: |
  cd $HOME/tmp/libb64-2.0.0/examples && make test; echo "exit=$?"
  /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -I../include -O2 -c ../src/cencode.c -o cencode.o && \
  /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -I../include -O2 -c ../src/cdecode.c -o cdecode.o && \
  /data/service/hnp/bin/llvm-ar rcs libb64.a cencode.o cdecode.o && \
  /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -I../include c-example1.c libb64.a -o c-example1 && ./c-example1

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: preserve-upstream-entry-and-run-equivalent-api-test
rec_description: >
  Preserve the failed upstream test entry as an upstream-entry result (record
  command, cwd, exit code 2, first stdout/stderr). Do not patch upstream. Then
  build src/cencode.c + src/cdecode.c with the OHOS clang toolchain into
  libb64.a and either compile the two official examples or an equivalent test
  that actually calls the public C API (encode/decode round-trip, helper
  length functions). Record every command/cwd/exit/log with SHA-256 and an
  explicit test ledger, separately from the upstream entry.
rec_command: |
  cd $HOME/tmp/libb64-2.0.0/examples && make test || echo "upstream_exit=2"
  /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -I../include -O2 -c ../src/cencode.c -o cencode.o
  /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -I../include -O2 -c ../src/cdecode.c -o cdecode.o
  /data/service/hnp/bin/llvm-ar rcs libb64.a cencode.o cdecode.o
  /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -I../include c-example1.c libb64.a -o c-example1 && ./c-example1
  /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -I../include c-example2.c libb64.a -o c-example2 && ./c-example2 loremgibson.txt encoded.txt decoded.txt && diff -q loremgibson.txt decoded.txt
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-recipe|test-package

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: document-ledger-only
fallback_description: >
  If an official example cannot run on OHOS (e.g. assertion mismatch or
  runtime limitation), keep it as a recorded entry with its real result and
  rely on the equivalent API-calling test in test_package/test_b64.c and
  test_harmonyos.c as the executable verification, with all entries listed in
  the ledger.
fallback_command: |
  cd $HOME/tmp/libb64-2.0.0 && /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -O2 -Iinclude -c src/cencode.c -o cencode.o && /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -O2 -Iinclude -c src/cdecode.c -o cdecode.o && /data/service/hnp/bin/llvm-ar rcs libb64.a cencode.o cdecode.o
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: test-package

forbid_1_pattern: "upstream make test passed with exit 0 in clean tree"
forbid_1_reason: In a clean source tree the upstream target exits 2; reporting 0 would be untruthful.
forbid_1_consequence: Test accounting fails audit; honest entry result is required.

forbid_2_pattern: "upstream tests: 0|未执行上游测试套件|no upstream tests exist"
forbid_2_reason: Upstream does expose a test target; counting zero without recording the attempted entry is under-reporting.
forbid_2_consequence: Knowledge audit rejects the pair as untraceable.

forbid_3_pattern: "replace make test with only a print-only test|include-only test"
forbid_3_reason: The replacement must actually call the library API (R34); a stub hides coverage.
forbid_3_consequence: Test quality gate fails.

principles: honest-test-accounting, preserve-failed-upstream-entry, equivalent-api-test, no-fake-tests, ohos-portability
